  "prefLabel": "We 207.02 Non-Adjudicative Public Hearings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 207.02 Non-Adjudicative Public Hearings. A non-adjudicative public hearing shall be held:\n\n(a) When proposing to adopt, readopt, amend, or repeal rules;\n\n(b) For any matter for which the board is required by law or by these rules to hold a hearing that is not a contested case; and\n\n(c) For any matter for which the law does not require the board to hold a hearing but for which the board believes a public hearing would be of benefit.\n\nSource. #7307, eff 6-13-00; ss by #9178-A, eff 6-13-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/we100-1000.html"
}
